1
00:00:00,148 --> 00:00:01,756
Sunlight is white.

2
00:00:01,778 --> 00:00:03,459
Space is black.

3
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:05,311
So why is the sky blue?

4
00:00:05,963 --> 00:00:08,274
That white light is really every color

5
00:00:08,148 --> 00:00:09,311
mixed together,

6
00:00:09,185 --> 00:00:11,015
each one a wave of a different

7
00:00:10,889 --> 00:00:11,904
length.

8
00:00:11,778 --> 00:00:13,533
When sunlight hits our air,

9
00:00:13,519 --> 00:00:16,570
tiny nitrogen and oxygen molecules scatter it.

10
00:00:16,519 --> 00:00:17,830
But they're picky:

11
00:00:17,704 --> 00:00:20,126
short blue waves scatter about five times

12
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,904
more than long red ones.

13
00:00:21,778 --> 00:00:23,904
So blue gets bounced all across the

14
00:00:23,889 --> 00:00:24,422
sky,

15
00:00:24,296 --> 00:00:26,941
and reaches your eyes from every direction.

16
00:00:26,889 --> 00:00:28,570
Violet is even shorter,

17
00:00:28,444 --> 00:00:30,570
so why not a purple sky?

18
00:00:30,497 --> 00:00:32,274
The Sun sends less violet,

19
00:00:32,148 --> 00:00:34,274
and your eyes are tuned to blue.

20
00:00:34,148 --> 00:00:35,311
At sunset,

21
00:00:35,185 --> 00:00:37,311
light crosses so much air that the

22
00:00:37,222 --> 00:00:38,830
blue is scattered away,

23
00:00:38,667 --> 00:00:40,941
leaving reds and oranges.

24
00:00:40,815 --> 00:00:42,163
Same air.

25
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,422
Same physics.

26
00:00:43,259 --> 00:00:44,459
Just sunlight…

27
00:00:44,296 --> 00:00:45,533
sorted by color.
